{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache and Vol. 3 felt like natural next choices because I want heavy riffs balanced with melody and memorable hooks, consistent with my interest in In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "The Sickness gives me a reason to explore more from Disturbed after Ten Thousand Fists, while Ascendancy appeals to the energetic, guitar-driven mood I associate with Advance And Vanquish."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger and Christ Illusion fit the heavy side of my listening, but their abrasive sound or relentless aggression misses the melodic balance I want today.",
    "Live In Texas misses my current interest in discovering studio albums; a related sound alone does not make a live set appealing right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat heaviness as enough of a connection, even though melody and hooks determine which heavy albums I actually want to hear.",
    "Sharing a broad musical neighborhood does not mean I would choose every album now: City of Evil, The War Within, and Mezmerize interest me, but fit my immediate mood less closely."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My interest in In Flames and Soilwork makes the balance between aggression and melody especially relevant to what I want next.",
    "My recent exploration of Ten Thousand Fists gives The Sickness a specific connection, while my current preference for studio recordings makes Live In Texas less appealing."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in heavy guitar music, but sometimes miss the melody, recording format, and immediate mood that guide my choices."
}"}
